WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.437
The federal requirement.

2
00:00:01.437 --> 00:00:06.013
The guide maps Gate 2 to NIST special
publication eight hundred fifty-three.

3
00:00:06.013 --> 00:00:10.205
A C five, separation of duties:
one approver system per class,

4
00:00:10.205 --> 00:00:12.601
and the requester never approves.

5
00:00:12.601 --> 00:00:15.390
C M three, configuration change control:

6
00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:19.025
each change class has a lane
and a change-record type.

7
00:00:19.025 --> 00:00:20.732
A C two, account management:

8
00:00:20.732 --> 00:00:25.387
one writer per attribute keeps account
changes traceable to the source.

9
00:00:25.387 --> 00:00:28.464
And Book 13 requires
the authorizing official

10
00:00:28.464 --> 00:00:31.225
to accept any autonomous class in writing.

11
00:00:31.225 --> 00:00:35.876
Chapter 08 maps the check to
configuration settings, change control,

12
00:00:35.876 --> 00:00:40.200
impact analysis, continuous
monitoring and system monitoring.

13
00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:45.455
The evidence an ISSO keeps: the attribute
map with each writer, the approver

14
00:00:45.455 --> 00:00:50.690
and lane tables, and the check's output
with the data architect's decisions.
